# PLC-Based Tank Level Control and Automation System
## OpenPLC Ladder Logic Design

**PLC Platform:** OpenPLC  
**Programming Language:** IEC 61131-3 Ladder Diagram (LD)  
**Development Environment:** OpenPLC Editor  
**Control Type:** Digital Input/Output Control

---

## 1. Introduction

This document describes the proposed Ladder Logic implementation of the tank-level control system.

The program is divided into functional networks covering:

1. Emergency stop and master enable
2. Tank-level status detection
3. Fault detection
4. Operating mode selection
5. Automatic filling
6. Manual draining
7. Output control and interlocking
8. Indicator lamps

The addresses used throughout this document follow the OpenPLC variable mapping.

**Notation:**

| Symbol | Description |
|---|---|
| `--| |--` | Normally open contact |
| `--|/|--` | Normally closed contact |
| `--( )--` | Output coil |
| `--(S)--` | Set/latch coil |
| `--(R)--` | Reset/unlatch coil |
| `TON` | On-delay timer |

